1: # Arbitrary-horizon PID measurement robustness: five goals proved
2: 
3: Complete: all five canonical goals in [Spec.v](../../problem/Spec.v) are proved by [Proof.v](Proof.v); pending requested goals: none. The main result is symbolic in E >= 0 and arbitrary natural n, with equal admissible initial integrals and fixed shared gains. For either horizontal axis, B=ceil(kp E/64), D_n<=min(187301888,n ki B), and for n>=1 both the stored and returned command difference are <=min(6432,B+ceil(n ki B/65536)). The separate zero-perturbation theorem gives exact equality, including every rounding boundary.
4: 
5: The active proof uses actual original Csem call sequences with explicit environment updates. Every call is bound to the existing exact normal-result theorem and uniqueness theorem, actual memory loads and returned fields. Exact signed-machine arithmetic correspondence precedes the clamp/ceiling inequalities and induction. Finite admissible input drivers have actual executions; all original reachable-state safety and all-successor termination conditions are retained. See the [canonical scope and unit interpretation](../../problem/report.md) for complete quantifiers, environment frames, numeric/memory conditions, concrete nonempty-domain feasibility argument and the physical 1cm illustration. The feasibility argument is explicitly distinguished from the five kernel-checked propositions.
6: 
7: The original C, model and prior attempts remain unchanged. This extends the existing guidance_pid_h_run_pos model and position-translation attempt 002; no new C/CBMC/model-generation stage was run. Hidden return-buffer ABI arguments are `[Vptr ret 0; Vint 1; Vptr gh 0]`. The inherited target is CompCert 3.17 x86-64 Linux little-endian, IEEE754 binary32 with round-to-nearest ties-to-even; checking uses Rocq 9.2. Integer loads observe exact machine words, including the active returned LTP command fields. Padding and inactive union bytes are not interpreted as command values. Environment frame uses `Mem.unchanged_on`; integral load preservation is explicit. The proof concerns original CompCert Csem, not a compiled hardware-binary correspondence theorem.
8: 
9: Original prepared C SHA-256: `8ca491f87de8559d9f4a48eca3fc7a70e63ac8edd7326e18483f25f2b5868c04`. Canonical Spec.v: `ce4faa4fec0b8994123d8d03b3e0a917c29faf22f2a9c3123470c4539169372e`. Proof.v: `c246c1ef03e0b07dc30d2bb8ec54c3f96a96aedf7bee685ef1b12337e345405c`. [provenance.json](provenance.json) pins the entire current source closure, model manifest, original prepare/align bindings and external semantic sources. [goal-validation.json](evidence/goal-validation.json) pins the actual compiled snapshots and exhaustive exact goal bindings. The checker verifies original handoff hashes and source stability before publication.
10: 
11: All 113 local source modules were cold compiled from immutable snapshots. Independent Proof kernel receipt: [proof-kernel-evidence.json](evidence/cold-checks/20261117T164424500354/proof-kernel-evidence.json), command `124-cold-independent-proof-kernel`. Exact typed [GoalBinding.v](evidence/cold-checks/20261117T164424500354/checked/paparazzi/relations/pid_measurement_robustness/attempts/001/GoalBinding.v) compiled with Print Assumptions, command `125-cold-exact-goalbinding`; its independent full-closure kernel passed, command `126-cold-exact-goalbinding-kernel`. Kernel receipt paths and original command logs are bound by goal-validation.json. All target source modules contain proofs, with no target Axiom/admit/Admitted. Inherited assumptions are the documented CompCert/Flocq baseline: ClassicalDedekindReals.sig_not_dec, sig_forall_dec, classical classic, dependent functional extensionality, proof irrelevance, and the standard Events.external_functions_sem/inline_assembly_sem parameters. No new axiom was introduced; the warm-cache/disabled-force domain follows internal original functions.
12: 
13: Reproduce from `/home/yangfp/five`: `source scripts/env.sh`, then `python3 paparazzi/relations/pid_measurement_robustness/attempts/001/check.py --timeout 600`. This repeats full cold compilation, both independent kernels and exact typed binding. `--publish` deliberately refreshes canonical receipts only after all checks and hash stability pass. Historical failed compile corrections are retained in the measured run logs; 11 failed helper/lead tool commands are indexed in [costs.json](costs.json), with no failed history erased.
14: 
15: Actual runtime model for all measured authoring/checking intervals is gpt-6.1-sol, requested and observed reasoning effort ultra; the explicit user request overrides the canonical medium default. [Runtime observations](evidence/runtime-config.json) cite each actual session. Five separate authoring/checking intervals include their own failures, repairs and successful checks. Mandatory initial skill/API reads before the lead boundary are identified instead of retrospectively assigned. Raw usage events, GNU time data and requested 10ms process-tree RSS sampling remain in each run. Cache/reasoning tokens are subsets, not additional totals. Shared pages may be counted twice and brief peaks missed; model-server/desktop memory and concurrent combined peak are unobserved. File-transfer/wrapper CPU/RSS is unobserved and not estimated.
